\section{1. Purpose}

The purpose of this Installation and Operational Qualification (IOQ) protocol is to provide documented evidence that {EQUIPMENTNAME} ({ASSETID}) has been installed in accordance with approved design, manufacturer, site, safety, utility, and documentation requirements and that it operates consistently throughout its defined operating ranges and intended functions.

Successful completion of this IOQ provides the documented basis for {NEXTQUALIFICATIONSTAGE}, subject to closure or formal acceptance of all deviations and open items.

\section{2. Scope}

This IOQ applies to {EQUIPMENTNAME}, including the main unit, identified components, controls, software/firmware where applicable, utilities, safety devices, alarms, interlocks, interfaces, and supporting documentation located at {LOCATION} within {SITENAME}.

Included scope: {INCLUDEDSCOPE}

Excluded scope: {EXCLUDEDSCOPE}

Interfaces covered by this protocol: {SYSTEMINTERFACES}

\section{3. Responsibilities}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
Role & Responsibilities
Equipment Owner / User & Define intended use and operating requirements; support execution; confirm SOPs and training; review results.
Engineering / Maintenance & Verify installation, utilities, drawings, safety, PM, spare parts, and technical support requirements.
Validation & Prepare or coordinate protocol, ensure traceability, oversee execution, assess deviations, and compile summary.
Quality Assurance & Approve the protocol and final qualification status; assess deviations and compliance impact as required.
IT / Automation (if applicable) & Support computerized-system configuration, user access, backup/restore, network, time synchronization, and data integrity testing.
Vendor / Supplier (if applicable) & Provide technical documentation, startup support, certificates, and agreed qualification evidence.
\end{tabular}

\section{4. Definitions and Abbreviations}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
Term & Definition
IOQ & Installation and Operational Qualification.
IQ & Installation Qualification: documented verification that installation and configuration meet approved requirements.
OQ & Operational Qualification: documented verification that the system operates as intended throughout specified operating ranges and challenge conditions.
URS & User Requirements Specification.
FAT / SAT & Factory Acceptance Test / Site Acceptance Test.
GDP & Good Documentation Practices.
GxP & Applicable regulated good-practice requirements.
CAPA & Corrective and Preventive Action.
N/A & Not Applicable; requires documented justification where used.
P/F & Pass / Fail.
\end{tabular}

