\section{7. Qualification Strategy and Acceptance}

The IOQ shall be executed using approved controlled documentation. Each test step shall be marked Pass or Fail based on the stated expected result. Objective evidence shall be attached or cross-referenced where required.

\begin{itemize}
\item All mandatory prerequisites are complete or formally approved to proceed with documented justification.
\item Each IQ and OQ test meets its acceptance criteria, or any exception is documented and assessed through the approved deviation process.
\item Critical deviations are closed before final IOQ approval unless an approved quality decision explicitly permits a defined conditional status.
\item All changes made during execution are assessed for impact and captured in the applicable change-control or deviation record.
\item Traceability between applicable requirements and qualification evidence is complete.
\end{itemize}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
Overall Acceptance Rule & {OVERALLACCEPTANCERULE}
Conditional Acceptance Rule & {CONDITIONALACCEPTANCERULE}
Critical Deviation Definition & {CRITICALDEVIATIONDEFINITION}
Retest Rule & {RETESTRULE}
\end{tabular}

