\section{9. Execution Instructions and Good Documentation Practices}

\begin{enumerate}
\item Execute the protocol in sequence unless a justified alternate sequence is documented.
\item Record results at the time the activity is performed. Do not leave data fields blank; enter N/A with justification where permitted by site procedure.
\item Use permanent, legible entries. Correct errors according to the approved site GDP procedure without obscuring the original entry.
\item Record instrument IDs for measuring devices used in qualification testing.
\item Attach or cross-reference objective evidence such as photographs, printouts, screenshots, calibration certificates, reports, logs, and vendor records.
\item If an expected result is not met, stop the affected test when appropriate, protect equipment/product/personnel, and initiate a deviation before continuing as defined by site procedure.
\item Retests shall be performed only after documented assessment and approved corrective action or rationale.
\item Any software, hardware, parameter, utility, or configuration change made during IOQ shall be documented and assessed for requalification impact.
\end{enumerate}
\begin{tabular}{llll}
Execution Start Date & {IOQSTARTDATE} & Execution End Date & {IOQENDDATE}
Protocol Copy No. & {PROTOCOLCOPYNO} & Controlled Copy Location & {CONTROLLEDCOPYLOCATION}
\end{tabular}

\section{10. Deviations and Exceptions}

Any departure from the approved protocol, expected result, approved configuration, or acceptance criterion shall be documented in the site deviation system. The qualification record shall cross-reference the deviation number and disposition.

\begin{tabular}{ll}
Deviation Classification & Definition / Handling
Critical & {CRITICALDEVIATIONHANDLING}
Major & {MAJORDEVIATIONHANDLING}
Minor & {MINORDEVIATIONHANDLING}
Protocol Exception / Editorial & {EXCEPTIONHANDLING}
\end{tabular}

