\section{12. Operational Qualification (OQ)}

OQ verifies that {EQUIPMENTNAME} operates according to approved requirements across defined operating ranges, control modes, alarms, interlocks, failure/recovery conditions, and data-handling functions as applicable.

\subsection{12.1 Power-Up, Startup, and Normal Shutdown}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
Test ID & 12.1
Requirement Ref. & {URSREFERENCE}
Objective & Verify controlled startup and shutdown sequences.
Preconditions & {PRECONDITIONS}
Acceptance Criteria & Equipment powers up, reaches ready state, and shuts down without unacceptable errors, hazards, or loss of required data.
Evidence / Attachment & {TESTEVIDENCE}
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llllll}
Step & Action / Challenge & Expected Result & Actual Result & P/F & Initials / Date
1 & Confirm prerequisites and utilities are available; switch equipment on using approved method. & Equipment starts and completes self-check/startup sequence successfully. & {F_121STEP1ACTUAL} & {F_121STEP1PF} & {F_121STEP1INITIALSDATE}
2 & Observe startup messages and system status. & Status indications are clear and no unexplained critical alarms are present. & {F_121STEP2ACTUAL} & {F_121STEP2PF} & {F_121STEP2INITIALSDATE}
3 & Place equipment into normal ready/idle state. & Equipment reaches defined state {READYSTATE}. & {F_121STEP3ACTUAL} & {F_121STEP3PF} & {F_121STEP3INITIALSDATE}
4 & Perform normal shutdown. & Equipment shuts down in controlled sequence and required records are retained. & {F_121STEP4ACTUAL} & {F_121STEP4PF} & {F_121STEP4INITIALSDATE}
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
Test Result & {F_121OVERALLPF} & Deviation No. & {F_121DEVIATIONNO}
